                    {
                        "form_id": "44788fd5-549c-4e25-9372-c58021b8601c",
                        "entry_id": "0d751a90-e11c-3dc1-9961-f8b39679c79c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "прися́гах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6e039fad-de6e-3c51-8b0f-e5a1e359335b",
                        "entry_id": "0d751a90-e11c-3dc1-9961-f8b39679c79c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "официальное торжественное обещание"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e5c085c-b978-4eab-a77d-7d83b1486f27",
                                "sense_id": "6e039fad-de6e-3c51-8b0f-e5a1e359335b",
                                "text": "В самое то же время приказано было всем полкам, всему духовенству, всем коллегиям и другим чиновникам, собраться к зимнему дворцу для учинения присяги императрице, которая и учинена всеми, не только без всякого прекословия, но всеми охотно и с радостию превеликою."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4aa6a89b-a1d4-4e2e-ad2e-fb419348fadc",
                                "sense_id": "6e039fad-de6e-3c51-8b0f-e5a1e359335b",
                                "text": "А если взглянуть на присяжных в момент принятия ими присяги, то по лицам видно, как они проникаются чувством ответственности за возложенную на них законом обязанность."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90df780c-b0fa-4894-a505-1c3deb6feccc",
                        "source_entry_id": "0d751a90-e11c-3dc1-9961-f8b39679c79c",
                        "source_sense_id": "6e039fad-de6e-3c51-8b0f-e5a1e359335b",
                        "target_lang_word": "oath",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "oath",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6389a60a-f7e7-3a28-afbe-d777a34cb399",
                                        "entry_id": "6d55f677-3cc3-39d1-b12a-9a6732944bb6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A solemn pledge or promise that invokes a deity, a ruler, or another entity (not necessarily present) to attest the truth of a statement or sincerity of one's desire to fulfill a contract or promise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98cc47e4-1b48-47b5-b48f-b43528c3bdbc",
                                                "sense_id": "6389a60a-f7e7-3a28-afbe-d777a34cb399",
                                                "text": "take an oath"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "054fdf8c-db20-4ae5-95f2-2fca7bd83000",
                                                "sense_id": "6389a60a-f7e7-3a28-afbe-d777a34cb399",
                                                "text": "swear an oath"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c634c20-1a7d-4cd1-b13a-36f589c3c4b8",
                                                "sense_id": "6389a60a-f7e7-3a28-afbe-d777a34cb399",
                                                "text": "break one's oath"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eddafb00-7036-4d48-8d08-57a0ea9ece2f",
                                                "sense_id": "6389a60a-f7e7-3a28-afbe-d777a34cb399",
                                                "text": "But all of us took an oath to do our duty when we joined the Space Force, and I fully expect everyone to willingly keep their word. But you took no oath, and have no obligation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1da4badc-ce93-4e51-81c6-ab764a2a40d4",
                                                "sense_id": "6389a60a-f7e7-3a28-afbe-d777a34cb399",
                                                "text": "There are […] brought all the way from Bougainville to present their birth certificates and testify in this courtroom, under oath, as to their given names."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "642ff7e1-54e2-3713-9d30-d2ef3831a23a",
                                        "entry_id": "6d55f677-3cc3-39d1-b12a-9a6732944bb6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A statement or promise which is strengthened (affirmed) by such a pledge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84bd2cda-0dfa-45ed-b02a-44a1034e7427",
                                                "sense_id": "642ff7e1-54e2-3713-9d30-d2ef3831a23a",
                                                "text": "After taking the oath of office, she became the country's forty-third premier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c83770d6-8773-4d4f-83b2-4e9d8008b9ff",
                                                "sense_id": "642ff7e1-54e2-3713-9d30-d2ef3831a23a",
                                                "text": "The generals swore an oath of loyalty to the country."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "181516e7-7a77-4b36-9fea-010ead91abbd",
                                                "sense_id": "642ff7e1-54e2-3713-9d30-d2ef3831a23a",
                                                "text": "Wrex: [sigh] Before I left, I made an oath to my father's father.\nWrex: I swore to recover my family's battle armor. It was taken from him after the uprising."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7124130f-a819-325d-b13c-42b597c56615",
                                        "entry_id": "6d55f677-3cc3-39d1-b12a-9a6732944bb6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A light, irreverent or insulting appeal to a deity or other entity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "274c82d7-646d-3a2e-a67b-a01ecb508b2b",
                                        "entry_id": "6d55f677-3cc3-39d1-b12a-9a6732944bb6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A curse, a curse word."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08dc83dc-89d3-4417-ba5c-9bc8a8ab87c9",
                                                "sense_id": "274c82d7-646d-3a2e-a67b-a01ecb508b2b",
                                                "text": "The farther from the Senator's office, the darker and older the furniture, the freer fly four-letter oaths, the higher the heaps of unfiled and unattended papers culminating in a frenzy of pulp in the press section[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "oath",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
